What are Wind Monopile Foundations?
Wind monopile foundations are the most widely used support structures for offshore wind turbines, consisting of single large-diameter steel pipe piles driven vertically into the seabed. These foundations dominate installations in shallow to moderate water depths (typically 30-40 meters) due to their structural simplicity, proven reliability, and cost-effectiveness compared to alternative solutions.
The transition piece connects the monopile to the turbine tower, creating a stable platform capable of withstanding harsh marine environments. Recent designs now accommodate next-generation turbines exceeding 15MW capacity, with diameters surpassing 9 meters in some installations.
